From c677586414c71f4d90b98dac800a9b616094efb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kx.zhou
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 14:40:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] clang: add Ascend CCE language extensions for clangd

Add support for Huawei Ascend CCE (Compute Core Engine) language extensions
to enable clangd IDE support for Ascend NPU kernel development.

Categories of changes:

1. Parser: Skip [aicore]/[aicpu]/[aicore,host] scope annotations.
2. Sema: Allow clang_builtin_alias for __builtin_cce_* builtins.
3. Type system: Add 8 CCE 8-bit floating-point builtin types plus __cce_half.
4. Kernel launch: Support the foo<<<numBlocks, smDesc, stream>>>(args) syntax.
   - Lexer emits <<< / >>> under the new CceExt language option (default on).
   - ActOnExecConfigExpr routes the exec config to bisheng's configure-call
     function __cce_rtConfigureCall (the same function ccec uses; see
     __clang_cce_runtime_wrapper.h), with signature
     unsigned int(unsigned int numBlocks, void *smDesc, void *stream),
     declared in the shim header. This enables argument-count and
     argument-type checking of the launch config.

The __fp8e6m2 type remains distinct from the other FP8 types. Constant
evaluation uses an editor-only E5M2 approximation.
